{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794646239,"nonce":"hFMWdvI6+1ml4TgmH/1+mHIwBd0=","message":"Timers and wakes under the iOS fiber, measured on the simulator as a .app (AOT, hlwindow 19f3a59, ash 028cf6a4). Ashui parks on window.wait(timeout), so this is the path that matters.\n\n- wait(0.5) in a loop for 3 s with no input: 6 timeouts in 11 waits. xwindow turns a finite wait into ControlFlow::WaitUntil, and winit schedules the wake, so ash arranges nothing.\n- 200 calls of wait(0.0): under 1 s.\n- A Haxe thread sets a flag and calls Window.wake() after 0.3 s while the program loops wait(5.0) until the flag is set: one call, ended in under 1.5 s.\n- Sys.sleep(0.3) on the program's own fiber: returns after 0.3 s, because the turn paces itself while the fiber is parked on something other than the host.\n\nNot covered: wait(-1) itself, a Haxe thread that stays a fiber on the main scheduler, Ashui's startup GPU awaits, a device.","files":null}]}